{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And the people.</b> This pericope follows sequentially, for after the ark set out from Mount Sinai they encamped at Kivrot HaTa'avah, and behold, he relates what occurred there." "<b>Like those who complain (כמתאוננים).</b> From the root און, likewise מחשבות אונך (Genesis 6:5)." "And the meaning of <b>and YHWH heard</b> — that they spoke words of און." "<b>And it consumed (ותאכל).</b> From the upper register [pa'el], like ויאמר, and by necessity from the lower register [pa'al] — the reverse of the usage; only thus we have found it."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {3 "The distinction between מלעיל and מלרע refers to conjugation patterns: מלעיל as the heavier/pi'el-type form, מלרע as the lighter/pa'al-type form. The argument is compressed and technically opaque; translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:17:07.236057287Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}